      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an e15 error code on the display. i checked the manual but i'm not really sure what to do next. how do i check the leak sensor and actually dry out the base?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "An E15 error on your Bosch dishwasher usually points to a leak detection issue, which is a bit like a low-level water-level alarm in the lower section of the machine. You'll need to check the drain pump area and the base for any signs of moisture, trying to locate where the water might be pooling. If you see standing water, you'll need to carefully wipe it out, ensuring the area around the pump and the drain hose is completely dry before running a test cycle again.\n\n**Disclaimer:** Since I am an AI and not a certified appliance technician, if you are uncomfortable inspecting the internal components, it might be best to call a professional, as some parts can be tricky to access.\n\n*If you're looking to check the leak sensor itself, it's often located near the base or under the tub, and sometimes it's a simple float switch or a sensor that gets triggered by water.*\n\n**For drying out the base:** After wiping down any visible water, you can run a hot rinse or a cleaning cycle with a dishwasher cleaner, leaving the door ajar afterward to promote airflow. This helps ensure any lingering dampness evaporates.\n\nIt's a delicate job, so proceed",
      "source": "target",
